+/**
+ * The public GitHub release feed for managed T3 releases, and the
+ * release-bound `ManagedArtifactSource` the runtime stager consumes.
+ *
+ * Discovery lists the fixed public repository, keeps the published, non-draft
+ * prereleases whose tag is exactly `t3-managed-v<managed version>`, and picks
+ * the highest managed version by SemVer precedence. Resolution reads that one
+ * release through its exact tag, downloads and verifies its two release
+ * documents with the real document verifier, proves the release's asset
+ * inventory is exactly the verified closure, and re-reads the tag so a release
+ * that moved while it was being read is refused rather than mixed.
+ *
+ * Every selection closes over one normalized release descriptor and the exact
+ * document bytes it verified. Its source never resolves "latest" again and
+ * never turns a caller- or manifest-supplied value into a network location:
+ * archive bytes come from the fixed asset-id endpoint for the pinned asset,
+ * after the descriptor has been proven unchanged once more.
+ *
+ * Pagination reads GitHub's `Link` header under a fixed-feed policy, not as a
+ * general RFC 8288 client: only the navigation relations `next`, `prev`,
+ * `first` and `last` are understood, and the one `next` target must be the
+ * fixed releases endpoint on the following page. Every other relation value
+ * and every other target is a refusal, so an unreadable continuation is an
+ * error rather than a silent end of the listing.
+ *
+ * Trust boundary, stated so nothing here is overclaimed:
+ *
+ * - The fixed HTTPS repository plus document and archive hashes give exact
+ *   byte identity under the trust placed in `kgarg2468/harbor` and GitHub.
+ *   There is no independent signature. A publisher or repository compromise
+ *   that replaces a release before this client first observes it is not
+ *   detectable here. Descriptor re-reads detect movement during one attempt;
+ *   the managed runtime's content record detects conflict with content this
+ *   host already published. GitHub's `immutable` release flag is exposed as
+ *   `githubImmutable` as an observation only; neither it, the 12-hex
+ *   release-input suffix in the version, nor `SHA256SUMS` is a trust root.
+ * - The queue persists only the exact `targetVersion` before staging
+ *   finishes, and a restarted process re-resolves it through `resolve`. The
+ *   selection-bound source prevents retargeting within one discovery/staging
+ *   attempt; durable pre-stage pinning of release id, asset id and document
+ *   hashes needs a later persistence change that this module does not make.
+ * - Wiring must keep one `ManagedReleaseSelection` paired with its `source`,
+ *   queue exactly `selection.version`, and require the stager's `artifactId`
+ *   to equal `selection.artifactId`. A later poll may yield a newer selection
+ *   but must not swap the source underneath an already queued target.
+ */
+
+export const MANAGED_RELEASE_REPOSITORY = "kgarg2468/harbor" as const;
+export const MANAGED_RELEASE_TAG_PREFIX = "t3-managed-v";
+
+const API_ORIGIN = "https://api.github.com";
+const RELEASES_PATH = `/repos/${MANAGED_RELEASE_REPOSITORY}/releases`;
+const RELEASES_URL = `${API_ORIGIN}${RELEASES_PATH}`;
